    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d2">

                <pb facs="0086" n="4" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg4"/>

                <head>Mr. Motley to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 79.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vienna,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 31, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to state that, upon the
                    26th of October, his Imperial Royal Majesty accepted the resignation by his
                    excellency Count Rechberg of his functions as minister of foreign affairs and of
                    the imperial household. The fact was communicated on the same day by circulars
                    to the various foreign legations at Vienna. On the following day a circular from
                    Count Mensdorff Ponilly announced his appointment to the functions resigned by
                    Count Rechberg.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to remain, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. LOTHROP MOTLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
